  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Munich Business School (MBS) is a prestigious private university located in the heart of Bavaria’s economic hub. Established in 1991, it was the first private university in Bavaria to receive state accreditation. You will find that MBS is dedicated to developing globally minded, innovative, and responsible business leaders. The university offers a range of business-focused programmes, from Bachelor’s and Master’s degrees to MBA and DBA options, all designed with a strong practical orientation and international focus.<br>&nbsp;</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p>You will experience a vibrant and inclusive community at MBS. With a high percentage of students coming from abroad, the campus is a melting pot of cultures. You can join various student-run initiatives such as the <strong>MBS International Club</strong>, which organises cultural events and activities, or the <strong>MBS Hiking Club</strong> to explore the beautiful Bavarian Alps. Other options include the <strong>MBS Dancing Club</strong> and <strong>MBS Chess Club</strong>, ensuring there is a space for your personal interests and networking outside the classroom.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>While MBS does not have traditional on-campus dormitories, you are supported through an exclusive partnership with <strong>Revo Munich Apartments</strong>. These fully furnished studio or duplex apartments are located just 20 minutes from the campus via the U5 line. They offer an all-inclusive rent model that covers internet, electricity, and heating. Additionally, the university provides a dedicated WhatsApp channel to help you find and connect with potential flatmates from the MBS community.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Facilities",
      "value": "<ol><li><strong>Library:</strong> The MBS library provides you with an inspiring environment for academic work. You will have access to a wide range of physical and digital business resources, databases, and quiet study spaces designed to support your research and project work.</li><li><strong>Sports:</strong> While the campus is boutique, you can engage in physical activities through student-led clubs like the <strong>MBS Hiking Club</strong>. Munich itself offers world-class sporting infrastructure, including the Olympic Park, where you can access various fitness facilities and outdoor tracks.</li><li><strong>Laboratories:</strong> MBS focuses on business and management, so you will find specialized <strong>Makers' Spaces</strong> and collaborative \"learning labs\" rather than traditional science laboratories. These spaces are equipped for prototyping, design thinking, and digital business simulations.</li><li><strong>Cafeteria:</strong> The campus features a central lounge area where you can relax between lectures. While there isn't a traditional large-scale canteen, the central location in Munich means you are surrounded by numerous cafes, bakeries, and restaurants offering diverse international cuisines.</li></ol>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Campuses",
      "value": "<p><strong>Munich (Elsenheimerstraße)</strong> The main campus is located in the Laim district of Munich. It is central, well-connected by public transport (U-Bahn and S-Bahn), and puts you right at the doorstep of major global corporations and start-ups. You will benefit from modern lecture halls, lounge areas, and proximity to the city's cultural attractions like the Marienplatz and English Garden.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
  ],
